{"entity":{"id":"cs:462","name":"British Togoland","dataset":"cshapes","kind":"polity"},"territories":[{"id":10383,"name":"British Togoland","set_id":"cs","class":"dependency","valid_from":1922.5479452054794,"valid_to":1956,"snapshot_held":0,"area_km2":26630.1,"border_precision":3,"capital_name":"Ho","sovereign":"United Kingdom","sovereign_note":"Derived: this territory lies inside \"Gold Coast\", which Historical Basemaps 1938 maps as subject to United Kingdom. CShapes' public file does not publish its status field.","modern_name":"Ghana","min_lon":-0.173605,"min_lat":6.212212,"max_lon":1.066839,"max_lat":11.101784,"source_file":"CShapes-2.0.geojson","source_row":"gwcode=462;start=1922-7-20"}],"identities":[{"qid":"Q797527","from_t":1922.5479452054794,"to_t":1956,"method":"name-label+date","confidence":0.95,"label":"British Togoland","description":"former territory under British administration","inception":1916.9863387978141,"dissolved":1956.948087431694,"enwiki":"British Togoland","summary":"British Togoland, officially Togoland under British Mandate and later officially the Togoland under United Kingdom Trusteeship, was a territory in West Africa under the administration of the United Kingdom, which subsequently entered a union with Ghana, part of which became its Volta Region. The territory was effectively formed in 1916 by the splitting of the German protectorate of Togoland into two territories, French Togoland and British Togoland, during the First World War. Initially, it was a League of Nations Class B mandate. In 1922, British Togoland was formally placed under British rule, and French Togoland, now Togo, was placed under French rule."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q797527","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q615006","value_label":"Ho","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Ho"},{"qid":"Q797527","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q1860","value_label":"English","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","ret